\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My heart and voice I raise,
\par To spread Messiah's praise;
\par Messiah's praise let all repeat;
\par The universe Lord,
\par By whose almighty word
\par Creation rose in from complete.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. A servant's from He wore,
\par And in His body bore
\par Our dreadful curse on Calvary:
\par He like a victim stood,
\par And poured His sacred blood,
\par To set the guilty captives free.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. But soon the Victor rose
\par Triumphant o'er His foes,
\par And led the vanquished host in chains:
\par He threw their empire down,
\par His foes compelled to own
\par O'er all the great Messiah reigns.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. With mercy's mildest grace,
\par He governs all our race
\par In wisdom, righteousness, and love:
\par Who to Messiah fly
\par Shall find redemption nigh,
\par And all His great deep profound,
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Hail, Saviour, Prince of Peace!
\par Thy kingdom shall increase,
\par Till all the world Thy glory see,
\par And righteousness abound
\par As the great deep profound,
\par And fill the earth with purity.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

